    "body": "The normal chain builder already handles this case in 3c65e18a2732ead7d61bec553d622a4d59c51f9e. It keeps one orientation-independent occurrence in the closed loop and reports each repeated primitive separately. It preserves the source drawing.\n\nThe regression `degenerate_pieces_are_refused_by_name` checks a reversed duplicate side and a preserved closed loop. A separate import and nominal geometry comparison confirmed the expected loop, including both distinct straight spans. My initial diagnosis counted the raw edges before this existing duplicate check.\n\nSelection of that valid loop for Wire Contour remains under #2022. The reentrant opening remains under #3178. No geometry repair change is required for this case.",
